# Trivy findings that are accepted for now.
#
# Rules for this file:
#   1. Every entry needs an expiry date and a reason. An entry without one is a
#      finding nobody owns.
#   2. Prefer `exp:` so the entry re-opens itself instead of ageing silently.
#   3. Suppress the narrowest thing that works - a single CVE, not a package.
#
# Format: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#by-finding-ids
#
# Example:
# CVE-2024-00000 exp:2026-12-31
#   No fix upstream; the affected code path is not reachable from our entrypoint.
#   Owner: platform-team. Re-checked 2026-09-08.
